 "best_diff": "--- initial\n+++ best\n@@ -19,7 +19,38 @@\n     features (they are standardized and a bias is added), so nonlinear structure only\n     helps if a feature expresses it. Only the Python standard library may be used.\n \n-    Current method: the raw inputs.\n+    Current method: log-transformed skewed features and selected pairwise products.\n     \"\"\"\n-    return list(row)\n+    x1, x2, x3, x4, x5, x6 = row\n+    \n+    # Log transform the skewed input x3\n+    log_x3 = math.log(x3 + 1e-8)  # Add small epsilon to avoid log(0)\n+    \n+    # Pairwise products for interaction terms (only some combinations)\n+    prod_12 = x1 * x2\n+    prod_13 = x1 * x3\n+    prod_23 = x2 * x3\n+    prod_45 = x4 * x5\n+    \n+    # Quadrant features using sign of products\n+    sign_12 = 1.0 if prod_12 > 0 else -1.0\n+    sign_23 = 1.0 if prod_23 > 0 else -1.0\n+    sign_45 = 1.0 if prod_45 > 0 else -1.0\n+    \n+    # Radius features (squared norms) for circular patterns\n+    radius_12 = x1**2 + x2**2\n+    radius_34 = x3**2 + x4**2\n+    radius_56 = x5**2 + x6**2\n+    \n+    # Thresholded features: soft step functions (tanh)\n+    thresh_3 = math.tanh(x3 - 1.0)  # Soft threshold around 1.0\n+    thresh_4 = math.tanh(x4 - 0.5)  # Soft threshold around 0.5\n+    \n+    return [\n+        x1, x2, log_x3, x4, x5, x6,      # Raw inputs and transformed\n+        prod_12, prod_13, prod_23, prod_45,   # Pairwise products\n+        sign_12, sign_23, sign_45,          # Sign of products\n+        radius_12, radius_34, radius_56,    # Squared radii\n+        thresh_3, thresh_4                  # Soft thresholds\n+    ]\n # OMEGA-BLOCK-END\n",
